# Depictio Tools Studio — env config. Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) for local
# runs, or set these in the Pages deploy workflow for production.

# --- Production OAuth one-click PR (see oauth-worker/README.md) ---
# The GitHub OAuth App client id (public) and the deployed worker's /exchange URL.
# When both are set, the Export step shows "Sign in with GitHub & open PR".
# When unset, it falls back to the zip + GitHub web-upload flow.
VITE_GH_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GH_OAUTH_WORKER_URL=

# --- Local testing only (DEV builds; ignored in production) ---
# Exercise the real fork/commit/PR flow without the worker or an OAuth App by
# supplying a short-lived token. IMPORTANT: .env files do NOT run shell, so put
# the ACTUAL token value here (a literal `$(gh auth token)` becomes the string
# "$(gh auth token)" → 401 Bad credentials). Easiest, from this dir:
#   echo "VITE_GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)" >> .env.local   # shell expands it
# then restart `pnpm dev` (Vite reads env only at startup). Needs `public_repo` scope.
# VITE_GH_TOKEN=ghp_xxx

# Optional: aim the PR at a throwaway repo so a local test doesn't hit
# depictio/depictio. Format: "owner/repo" or "owner/repo@branch".
# VITE_GH_TARGET=your-user/catalog-sandbox
